BT 1 0 0 1 0 60.2 Tm 11.5 TL /F1 8.8 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Thus a time series analysis and forecast was carried out on the monthly airline passenger data \(144 months, 1949-1960\). The) Tj T* (series showed a rising trend and yearly seasonality \(peak in July, low in November\) and was non-stationary \(ADF p = 0.9919\). One) Tj T* (difference was not enough \(p = 0.0542\), while the second difference was stationary \(p < 0.0001\), so d = 2 was used. An ARIMA\(1,) Tj T* (2, 2\) model, chosen by lowest AIC, was fitted on the first 115 months and used to forecast the last 29 months, giving MSE) Tj T* (16,799.32, MAE 115.32 and RMSE 129.61. The forecast follows the trend but misses the seasonal swings, so a seasonal ARIMA) Tj T* (model is recommended for better accuracy.) Tj T* ET
